uid", 3347640, 1764], ["Printed_HX", 3354696, 288], ["Aux_Vapour", 3355848, 1488], ["Aux_Liquid", 3361800, 1488]]}, {"name": "OPF_REF_Bay_Envelope", "coll": "OPFPLG_Reference", "pivot": [0.0, 0.65, -0.82], "pos": [3367752, 8], "groups": [], "edges": [3367848, 24]}, {"name": "OPF_REF_Pusher_Duct_L", "coll": "OPFPLG_Reference", "pivot": [0.45, 0.79913, -2.27592], "pos": [3367944, 1218], "groups": [["Ref_Duct", 3382560, 3648]]}, {"name": "OPF_REF_Pusher_Duct_R", "coll": "OPFPLG_Reference", "pivot": [-0.45, 0.79913, -2.27592], "pos": [3397152, 1218], "groups": [["Ref_Duct", 3411768, 3648]]}], "report": "X1 OPFPLG 1,500 hp - lightweight build: 150 bore x 124 stroke per piston, 13.1 L, aluminium windings, printed block\n  bore 150 mm, stroke 124 mm per piston, 3 cylinders x 2 pistons, 13.1 L swept, compression ratio 16:1 after port closure\n  CYCLE MODEL (opf_cycle.py), continuous point: 44.9 Hz, mean piston speed 11.1 m/s, scavenge 3.80 bar abs, lambda 1.79, IMEP 21.5 bar, peak 225 bar\n    fuel 2472 kW (53.3 g/s propane) -> indicated 51.4 % -> stators 1141 kW -> DC link 1124 kW\n    e-turbo: compressor 329 kW at PR 3.96, turbine 347 kW at 792 K, net +11 kW to the DC link\n    NET 1132 kW = 1519 hp continuous at 45.8 % fuel-to-DC; 200 lb of propane lasts 28 min at this power\n    burst point (scavenge 4.1 bar, lambda 1.60): 1900 hp from the engine, peak 247 bar; with the LTO pack (413 hp for 10 s) the 2,000 hp ceiling is covered\n  LINEAR GENERATOR (per piston): double-sided magnet sleeve 251 mm dia x 175 mm, 6 poles, moving mass 14.7 kg (magnets 10.1 kg)\n    stators: cobalt-iron cores, aluminium windings in 24 mm slots; outer stator covers 99 / 95 / 60 % of the sleeve at inner / mid / outer dead centre\n    air-gap area 0.265 m2 (0.207 m2 working at mid stroke; inner stator covers 93 / 59 / 23 % at inner / mid / outer dead centre)\n    force 16.0 kN rms, 28.0 kN peak; air-gap shear 82 kPa rms against the 85 kPa continuous yardstick: margin x1.03\n    peak shear 121 kPa against 170 kPa short-term: margin x1.40\n    winding loss 3.9 % of converted power (7.8 kW per piston into boiling propane), core loss 1.8 %\n    motor alone, bounce chamber vented: can drive a full compression stroke x1.05 at full boost, x4.0 at start (compression work 3.14 kJ)\n    peak gas load 398 kN is carried by piston inertia (as in every free-piston engine), not by the machine\n    recommended DC link 900 V (SiC), tied to the 373 V LTO pack through the deck DC/DC\n  PROPANE CHAMBERS (one per piston): gas volume 15.9 -> 13.8 L, pressure 22.4 -> 26.3 bar each stroke (boils at 63-71 C)\n    heat per circuit 56 kW (crown + liner 36, stators 11.4, friction 3.5, bounce losses 5.8) -> 215 g/s of vapour, 4 % of the swept volume bled per stroke\n    condenser side held near 23.8 bar (66 C): liquid enters through the check valve at the low end of the swing, vapour leaves through the bleed valve at the high end\n  CHARGE AIR COOLER: 1.79 kg/s from 212 C to 62 C, 271 kW into the two auxiliary circuits (148 kW each with the inverter cold plates)\n  HEAT REJECTION: 633 kW total, 316 kW per pusher; at 60 m/s through the duct (24 kg/s) the air warms 13 K\n    fin area needed per pusher: 31 m2 on a 15 C day, 62 m2 on a 35 C day; a pack of thin cambered fins filling the annulus 140 mm deep holds about 56 m2 (no thick vanes)\n  MOVING CLEARANCES: crowns 12 mm apart at the inner dead centre; carrier disc 10 mm from the liner end and magnet sleeve 9 mm from the housing wall there; disc 16 mm from the end cap at the outer dead centre; 103 % of the skirt still in the liner there   OK\n  CENTRE BLOCK: one printed aluminium piece 276 mm wide x 1108 mm long x 364 mm tall with the three bores, port galleries and a propane cooling gallery through each combustion zone; six stator assemblies bolt to its two faces, 16 x M8 each, carrying about 216 kN of chamber pressure load per joint\n  MASS ESTIMATE (built up from this geometry, about +/-20 %):\n    stators 262 kg (outer 30 + inner 14 per piston), moving parts 88 kg\n    printed aluminium block and casing 113 kg: bore walls and galleries 28, generator housings 51, block skin, bolt faces, webs and mounts 25, fasteners 9\n    ENGINE 472 kg; with air path 72, electronics 90, cooling 86 and LTO pack 102: PACKAGE 823 kg (1814 lb)\n  FIT in the X1 SkyRacer (craft coordinates, m):\n    cylinders + generators x: -0.496 .. +0.496   bay box -0.500 .. +0.500   margin +4 mm   OK\n    cylinders + generators y: +0.145 .. +1.253   bay box +0.140 .. +1.500   margin +5 mm   OK\n    cylinders + generators z: +0.510 .. +0.874   bay box +0.420 .. +0.880   margin +6 mm   OK\n    e-turbo: aft of the cylinders to y 1.625 (+125 mm past the old bay box, still ahead of the pushers); skin clearance sides +69 mm, belly +69 mm\n    charge air cooler (spine, between the wing roots) and electronics deck (ahead of the wing): +22 mm under the outer skin line\n    under the rear wing root (estimated lower surface): closest part OPF_Exhaust_Collector at +17 mm\n  accumulator (unchanged): 162 x Toshiba SCiB 20Ah-HP LTO, 162S, 373 V nominal, 7.5 kWh, ~308 kW for 10 s; housings 10 mm above its lid   OK\n  RESULT: fits - cylinders inside the bay box; e-turbo, cooler, deck and line trays are outside the old box but inside the skin; pusher lines, condensers and tailpipe are external by design", "fits": true, "design": {"B": 0.15, "S": 0.12375, "disp": 0.01312105806725862, "m_move": 14.71554807287919, "F_cont": 17564.986174421607, "F_pk": 35129.972348843214, "Lm": 0.1752499999999999, "r_mo": 0.12550000000000003, "r_ho": 0.16600000000000004, "zc": 0.6920000000000001, "y_T": 1.4565000000000001, "z_T": 0.64, "Vb_idc": 0.01594374171670789, "Vb_odc": 0.013756898705498118, "A_eff": 0.20664689616966597, "END": 0.496, "pitch": 0.3720000000000001, "clear": {"crowns_idc": 0.0125, "disc_liner_idc": 0.010499999999999954, "sleeve_wall_idc": 0.009000000000000008, "skirt_disc": 0.14024999999999993, "disc_cap_odc": 0.016000000000000014, "seal_cover": 0